#
# A genuinely-gluing global section over a NON-IDENTITY math:SheafRestrictionMap: the
# general cellular-sheaf gluing condition is restriction(sourceValue) = targetValue, of
# which the raw source/target agreement other fixtures in this suite exercise is only the
# identity-map special case (a math:ConstantSheaf). Here the restriction map's declared
# math:RestrictionImage records a genuinely non-identity action — it sends the source
# value 3 to 6, a doubling — and the target stalk carries the value 6, so applying the
# map to the source value agrees with the target: restriction(3) = 6 = 6. The section
# still glues (math:SectionGluingInconsistency inert) even though 3 ≠ 6 raw, proving the
# corrected constraint checks the TRANSPORTED value, never the raw source, against the
# target.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/gluing-nonidentity/> .

ex:sheaf a math:CellularSheaf ;
    math:sheafBaseComplex ex:base ;
    math:hasStalk ex:vertexStalk , ex:edgeStalk ;
    math:restrictionMap ex:vertexToEdge ;
    math:hasGlobalSection ex:globalSection .
ex:base a math:CellComplex .
ex:subregion a math:CellComplex .

# The source stalk carries 3; the target stalk carries 6 — NOT raw-equal to the source,
# but exactly the image the non-identity restriction map declares for that source value.
ex:vertexStalk a math:SheafStalk ; math:stalkOverCell ex:vertex ; math:stalkValue 3 .
ex:edgeStalk a math:SheafStalk ; math:stalkOverCell ex:edge ; math:stalkValue 6 .
ex:vertexToEdge a math:SheafRestrictionMap ;
    math:sourceObject ex:vertexStalk ;
    math:targetObject ex:edgeStalk ;
    math:restrictionImage ex:vertexToEdgeImage .

# The non-identity action: restriction(3) = 6, a doubling — NOT the identity map.
ex:vertexToEdgeImage a math:RestrictionImage ;
    math:imageSourceValue 3 ; math:imageTargetValue 6 .

# The global section over the ENTIRE base — the map's declared image (3 ↦ 6) agrees
# with the target stalk's declared value (6), so it glues.
ex:globalSection a math:GlobalSection ;
    math:overSheaf ex:sheaf ;
    math:sectionRegion ex:base .

# A local section over a proper subcomplex — legitimately scoped smaller.
ex:localSection a math:LocalSection ;
    math:overSheaf ex:sheaf ;
    math:sectionRegion ex:subregion .

# The H¹ obstruction class, anchored to the sheaf whose lifting it reasons about.
ex:gluingObstruction a math:GluingObstruction ;
    math:obstructionOf ex:sheaf .

ex:vertex a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:edge a math:MathematicalObject .
